<question type="stack">
  <name><text>A point in a region defined by three conditions</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\(A\) is \(({@A[1]@}, {@A[2]@})\) and \(B\) is \(({@B[1]@}, {@B[2]@})\). Give a point \(P\) with whole-number coordinates such that \(PA \lt {@r1@}\), \(PB \lt {@r2@}\) and \(P\) is nearer to \(A\) than to \(B\).</p><div>\(P = \big(\)[[input:ans1]], [[input:ans2]]\(\big)\) [[validation:ans1]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The region is inside the circle with centre \(A\), radius \({@r1@}\), inside the circle with centre \(B\), radius \({@r2@}\), and on \(A\)'s side of the perpendicular bisector of \(AB\). All three boundaries are dashed, because the inequalities are strict. Test a point by comparing squares: \(PA^2 \lt {@r1^2@}\), \(PB^2 \lt {@r2^2@}\) and \(PA^2 \lt PB^2\).</p><p>For example \(P({@tp[1][1]@}, {@tp[1][2]@})\): \(PA^2 = {@(tp[1][1]-A[1])^2+(tp[1][2]-A[2])^2@}\), \(PB^2 = {@(tp[1][1]-B[1])^2+(tp[1][2]-B[2])^2@}\). There are \({@ng@}\) points with whole-number coordinates in the region.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* Design: give a point in a region defined by three conditions; any point in the region scores. Entries [A, B, r1, r2]: 10 to 16 lattice points in each region, A itself not in it, no two the same shape. Test points [correct, correct, fails 1, fails 2, fails 3]. Source: original. */
q73: [[[0,1],[6,0],4,6],[[0,-2],[5,-3],4,5],[[-3,0],[4,-1],5,6],[[-1,1],[6,3],5,6],[[0,1],[5,2],4,5],[[-2,-2],[4,-1],4,6],[[-3,0],[4,0],5,6],[[-1,-1],[5,1],4,6],[[1,1],[7,-1],4,6],[[1,-2],[8,-1],5,6]];
q73t: [[[1,-2],[3,3],[1,-3],[-3,-1],[3,-1]],[[1,-5],[2,0],[3,1],[-3,-4],[2,-5]],[[-1,-4],[0,3],[1,4],[-7,-2],[1,-2]],[[1,0],[3,0],[1,6],[-5,-1],[2,4]],[[1,0],[2,3],[3,-2],[-3,-1],[2,4]],[[-1,-4],[1,-2],[-1,2],[-5,-4],[1,-1]],[[-1,-3],[0,3],[0,-4],[-7,-2],[1,-2]],[[0,-2],[2,-1],[0,3],[-4,-3],[2,0]],[[2,-2],[4,3],[2,-4],[-2,-1],[4,-1]],[[3,-4],[4,1],[5,-6],[-3,-4],[5,-4]]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
A: q73[ix][1]; B: q73[ix][2]; r1: q73[ix][3]; r2: q73[ix][4];
tp: q73t[ix];
ta1: tp[1][1]; ta2: tp[1][2];
ng: length(sublist(create_list([u,w], u, -12, 14, w, -12, 12), lambda([z], is((z[1]-A[1])^2+(z[2]-A[2])^2<r1^2 and (z[1]-B[1])^2+(z[2]-B[2])^2<r2^2 and (z[1]-A[1])^2+(z[2]-A[2])^2<(z[1]-B[1])^2+(z[2]-B[2])^2))));]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
